<p>Second album in the original cycle, produced by <strong>Fábio “Badi” Crepaldi</strong> and Marcelo Nicchio, who also recorded drums.</p><p>The recording revisited emblematic songs from the band through the aesthetics of that period, introduced new compositions by Nicchio and included a ska/punk/reggae version of <em>Ciúmes</em>, by <strong>Ultraje a Rigor</strong>.</p><p>Released on CD in <strong>2000</strong>, the work opened new opportunities for media appearances and live performances.</p><figure class="thread-media thread-media--linked"><a aria-label="Open the Eu Não Tô Nem Aí cover at full size" href="/assets/archive/music/coitado-do-proximo/2000-eu-nao-to-nem-ai/coitadodoproximo_00_eunaotonemai_2000_01_capa.jpg" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><img alt="Cover of Eu Não Tô Nem Aí, Coitado do Próximo’s second album, released in 2000." decoding="async" loading="lazy" src="/assets/archive/music/coitado-do-proximo/2000-eu-nao-to-nem-ai/coitadodoproximo_00_eunaotonemai_2000_01_capa.jpg" width="1254" height="1254"/></a><figcaption><strong>Eu Não Tô Nem Aí · 2000.</strong><span class="thread-media-note">Cover of Coitado do Próximo’s second album.</span><a class="thread-media-open" href="/assets/archive/music/coitado-do-proximo/2000-eu-nao-to-nem-ai/coitadodoproximo_00_eunaotonemai_2000_01_capa.jpg" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Open image at full size ↗</a></figcaption></figure><!-- gallery:eu-nao-to-nem-ai-2000:start -->
